WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.320
Back in the '90s, there weren't many comedians
quite as big as Jeff Foxworthy.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.800
His relatable humor about being a regular
guy from the South endeared him to millions…and

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.019
so did his extremely popular "you might be
a redneck" jokes.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.740
"My definition of redneck, it is a glorious
absence of sophistication."

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.660
Foxworthy's albums sold so well that he became
the most successful comedy recording artist

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.580
of all time.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:27.320
He also starred in his own network sitcom,
hosted Are You Smarter Than a Fifth Grader?

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:31.120
and headlined the Blue Collar Comedy Tour
with Bill Engvall, Larry the Cable Guy, and

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:31.700
Ron White.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.440
Today, Foxworthy isn't the white-hot king
of comedy he once was, but he's still got

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.240
a huge following and keeps very busy.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.720
Here's what he's been up to lately.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.660
Becoming a salesman

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.100
Fans might not see Foxworthy's shows or stand-up
specials while flipping through the channels

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.520
as much as they used to, but they can still
catch a glimpse of him on TV.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:54.680
Since 2015, Foxworthy has been the face and
voice of the Golden Corral buffet chain.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.620
He's also made ads for Purina deer chow and
the iScope, an iPhone attachment that allows

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.580
hunters to take videos of whatever they see
through their gun's sight.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:07.320
Most of these products fit into his down home
aesthetic, and he's also got his own marketplace

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.160
in play as well.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:13.060
In 2011, he also started his own sports equipment
company called Foxworthy Outdoors.The company

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:18.380
sells a wide array of gear, including Jeff
Foxworthy Beef Jerky and "Redneck"-themed

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.340
T-shirts of course.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:24.220
The storefront is also an umbrella under which
Foxworthy produces his series Inside &amp; Out.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.200
But he's not just in the business of selling
stuff these days.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.400
Turning to philanthropy

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:33.960
For a guy who positioned himself as such a
salt-of-the-earth type of person, it's only

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.020
natural that he should put his money where
his mouth is.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.300
So, Foxworthy has made good use of his fame
and fortune over the years by investing in

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.880
several charitable endeavors.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.240
It starts at home, as Foxworthy Outdoors helps
fund hunting trips on Foxworthy's land preserve

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.180
for wounded soldiers and children with life-threatening
illnesses.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:55.880
Plus, in 2012, he granted a local land trust
a conservation easement over 1000 acres of

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.540
his property in Georgia to protect the property
from construction.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.740
And for more than a decade, the comedian and
his family have worked with a humanitarian

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:07.840
aid organization called Compassion International,
even traveling to Rwanda to help in and around

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.320
the organization's development center.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:15.300
Another cause Foxworthy goes out of his way
to support is Cure Childhood Cancer, an organization

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.620
based near his home in Atlanta.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:20.720
And for locals around his hometown, he's been
known to pick up the tab on a grocery bill

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:21.920
when things got tight, too.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:23.880
Continuing his career

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.000
While it might seem like Jeff Foxworthy has
disappeared from the spotlight, he's still

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:28.640
very busy.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.580
Logging all those hours on the stage and on
TV made Foxworthy's voice as recognizable

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:38.090
as his face and name, so in recent years,
he's lent his high-pitched drawl to a bunch

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:43.400
of animated projects, including The Smurfs,
Hatched, Ozzy, and Bunyan and Babe.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.540
"Well, I'll be smurfed."

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:51.820
And in 2013, CMT aired 13 episodes of Bounty
Hunters, an animated sitcom about a small-town

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:56.900
bail bonds business starring Foxworthy alongside
his old Blue Collar Comedy Tour-mates.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.920
Plus, after hosting Are You Smarter than a
Fifth Grader? for five seasons, Jeff Foxworthy

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.380
continued to frequent the reality competition
circuit as well.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.740
He appeared in in two episodes of ABC's Shark
Tank and headlined the American adaptation

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.360
of Britain's The Great British Bake Off for
a single season at CBS.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:17.020
He also hosted The American Bible Challenge,
which tested people's familiarity with the

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:17.760
titular book.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.820
Meanwhile, his stand-up career is still ticking
along strong, too.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:25.181
Foxworthy continues to tour the nation with
his signature phrases, playing a number of

00:03:25.181 --> 00:03:28.120
dates each year at fairs, comedy clubs, and
casinos.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:33.700
And in 2017, he co-headlined Jeff &amp; Larry's
Backyard BBQ tour with Larry the Cable Guy.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.840
The pair also teamed up to make a special
for Netflix called We've Been Thinking, wherein

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.300
he announced that he might have a new career
path altogether in mind.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.900
"Well, I haven't decided if I'm running for
President or not yet…"

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.040
In other words, we haven't heard the last
of Jeff Foxworthy just yet.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:52.660
Thanks for watching!

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.400
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.580
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

